# ─── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Wildcarded rather than enumerated: the list was four fixed names, so every new
# configuration (a stress build, an -icount build) showed up as untracked until
# someone remembered to add it.
cmake-build-*/
tests/build/
stress_tests/build/
build/
tools/__pycache__
profile/
compile_commands.json
test.img

# ─── Editor / IDE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.zed/

# ─── macOS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store

# ─── Specs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The spec tree is internal to the design process, not a published artifact:
# working documents with open items, referee rounds and in-flight amendments,
# read alongside the .claude/skills spec workflow. The committed record of what
# was decided and why lives in docs/ instead.
specs/

# ─── Benchmarking rulers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Vendored third-party baseline code (Linux's maple tree + shims, GPL-2.0) used
# only to measure against. License-incompatible with the tree, so it must never
# enter history — same arrangement as specs/: on disk, never committed.
bench-maple/

# ─── Local scripts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
tools/cloc-main.sh

# ─── Claude Code ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Personal overrides only. .claude/settings.json and .claude/skills/ are
# deliberately NOT ignored — the skills directory holds this project's spec
# workflow (spec-init / refine / review / resolve / implement / status), which
# is shared tooling rather than local state.
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.md
